dacp: authorize a speaker's own requests without trusted_networks

An AirPlay 2 receiver reports its physical volume buttons back to the
sender over DACP (/ctrl-int/1/setproperty?dmcp.device-volume=...),
identifying itself with the Active-Remote the sender put in the RTSP
session. dacp_request_authorize() only accepted a trusted peer or a
DAAP session, so with `trusted_networks = { "localhost" }` every such
request was refused with 403 and the speaker's buttons never reached
the player. The workaround, listing the speaker's address in
trusted_networks, also opens the JSON API and DAAP to that address,
and goes stale whenever the address changes.

Accept a DACP request when its Active-Remote names a known output and
the request comes from that output's address. The player already
knows both, so nothing has to be configured and an address change is
picked up with the next mDNS resolve. The exposure is the same as
trusting the address, minus everything that is not DACP.

